# {{KIT_NAME}}

A prototyping playground for {{DS_NAME}}. You describe a screen in one sentence; Claude
builds it with the real {{DS_NAME}} tokens and components, ready to click through in a
browser. Prototypes here are throwaway: they answer a question, they are not products.

## Start

```bash
cd {{KIT_NAME}}
claude
```

Claude starts the dev server itself. To run it by hand: `pnpm dev` (first time: `pnpm install`).
You need Node 22.22 or newer and pnpm (`npm i -g pnpm`); `pnpm dev` checks both first and tells
you exactly what is missing.

## Ask

Talk to Claude in plain language. Three kinds of requests work well:

- **Build a prototype:** "Build a prototype of a checkout page: delivery address form on the left, order summary on the right, with an error state for an invalid postcode."
- **Explore ideas:** "Explore three different ideas for how a customer could renew a subscription; keep them rough and side by side."
- **Extend an existing prototype:** "Extend the checkout prototype: add a coupon field and show what happens when the code is invalid."

Name real content, states, and the question you want answered. The more concrete the sentence,
the more the prototype can tell you.

## Look

- **The overview:** http://localhost:{{PORT}} lists every prototype by title, groups explorations
  under "Ideas", and has an Auto / Desktop / Mobile toggle to open any prototype in a 375 px
  device frame.
- **The reference screen:** http://localhost:{{PORT}}/#/p/{{REFERENCE_SLUG}}, marked "Reference" on
  the overview. This is what {{DS_NAME}} is supposed to look like in this kit; judge every
  prototype against it.
- **The components overview:** http://localhost:{{PORT}}/#/p/{{REFERENCE_SLUG}}/components shows
  every component with its variants and states on one screen.

## Share

```bash
pnpm export --only <slug>
```

produces `export/index.html`: one file containing just that prototype (the slug is shown on
each overview card). It opens offline by double-click, so it can be sent as is. `pnpm export`
alone bundles every prototype into one file.

Tip: ask Claude to "publish export/index.html as a Claude Artifact" for a private link you can
share without sending a file.

